<title>MEXICO: Mexico's silver output slides higher Jan-April.</title>
<headline>Mexico's silver output slides higher Jan-April.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest refined silver producer, produced 854,525 kg of silver in the first four months of the year, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of other metals and mineral production follows.  </p>
<p>    Product    April 97   April 96   Jan-Apr 97  Pct Yr/Yr Chg</p>
<p>    Gold	   2,318	2,022	 8,503	  +8.8</p>
<p>    Silver     215,025    210,553     854,525	  +1.8</p>
<p>    Lead	  12,590     12,017	61,528	 +21.0</p>
<p>    Copper	30,326     28,690     105,008	  -6.6</p>
<p>    Zinc	  27,751     28,360     118,157	  +8.1</p>
<p>    Coal	 809,536    645,367   3,071,488	 +23.2</p>
<p>    Iron	 442,458    488,323   1,962,224	  -4.4</p>
<p>    Sulphur     67,982     76,030     290,305	  -9.1</p>
<p>    Gypsum     416,249    276,054   1,382,825	 +26.3</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 60,300     57,317	51,757	   n/d</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals in kilos, others in tonnes. Coal measured in mineral volume.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Redaccin Mxico +525 728 9530))</p>
